    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2025681498028867683",
      "url": "https://x.com/rst_cloud/status/2025681498028867683",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/rst_cloud/status/2025681498028867683",
      "text": "#threatreport #HighCompleteness\nGhost in Your Network: How Earth Kurma Stays Hidden and Exfiltrates Your Data | 20-02-2026\nSource: https://t.co/M5a6lClUFK\nKey details below ↓\n\n🧑‍💻Actors/Campaigns:\nEarth_kurma\nToddycat\nLancefly\nTunnelsnake\nSharppanda\n\n💀Threats:\nNbtscan_tool, Ladon_tool, Frpc_tool, Kmlog_tool, Krnrat, Moriya, Mmload, Dunloader, Tesdat, Dmloader, Downbegin, Wmihacker_tool, Odriz_tool, Simpoboxspy_tool, Simpowebexspy, Downtown, Cobalt_strike_tool, Vikturi, Victorydll, \n🎯Victims: Southeast asia\n\n🏭Industry: Telco, Government\n\n🌐Geo: Philippines, Asia, Indonesia, Malaysia, Thailand, Vietnam\n\n📚TTPs:\n⚔️Tactics: 6\n🛠️Technics: 0\n\n🧨IOCs:\n - Command: 10\n - Path: 13\n - File: 34\n - IP: 11\n - Email: 1\n - Hash: 33\n - Domain: 1\n\n💽Software: Dropbox, Windows Filter Manager, Windows Security, Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel\n\n🔢Algorithms: zip, xor, sha256\n\n🗂️Win API: NetBIOS, NtCreateThreadEx, ObRegisterCallbacks, PsSetLoadImageNotifyRoutine, PsSetCreateProcessNotifyRoutine, SwitchToFiber, WaitForMultipleObjects\n\n📜Programming Languages: powershell\n\n💻Platforms: x64\n\n#threatreport:\nEarth Kurma is a sophisticated advanced persistent threat (APT) group that has been active since November 2020, primarily targeting Southeast Asia. The group exhibits a strong focus on data exfiltration, utilizing advanced techniques for evasion and persistence. Their operations have shown weak ties to other known APT groups like ToddyCat and Lancefly, further indicating their unique methodology.\n\nThis APT employs various tools for lateral movement, including NBTSCAN for NetBIOS scanning, LADON for intranet penetration, and WMIHACKER for lateral movement facilitation. In terms of persistence mechanisms, Earth Kurma utilizes multiple rootkits, backdoors, and loaders. Among their key tools is KRNRAT, a comprehensive backdoor leveraging several open-source projects. Its user-mode agent is injected into \"svchost.exe\" and operates in a memory-resident manner. Similarly, they use MORIYA, a traffic interceptor that hides malicious payloads within TCP traffic, specifically targeting packets based on their initial bytes for injection.\n\nEarth Kurma's arsenal includes multi-stage, reflective-loading rootkits capable of backdoor operations and memory-resident agents that utilize legitimate services like Cisco Webex and DFSR for command and control communication as well as malware deployment. They have developed a variety of custom loaders and backdoors, such as DOWNBEGIN, which operates through rundll32.exe, offering numerous command capabilities for file management and C&C communication. This variant is particularly notable for its function of creating multiple Cisco Webex meeting rooms to facilitate communication with compromised systems.\n\nThe group also utilizes SIMPOBOXSPY, a straightforward tool for uploading files to services like Dropbox, highlighting their reliance on legitimate platforms to exfiltrate data. The variety in their tools—including the reflective-loading capabilities and the specific commands used for file operations—reveals a well-thought-out attack strategy that focuses on both stealth and effectiveness. Earth Kurma's sophisticated methodologies exemplify the ongoing evolution of cyber threats, stressing the need for continuous vigilance and adaptation in security measures.",
